if you're using LinkedIn to drive people toward your technical content.

If by “blog” you mean a static technical blog hosted on GitHub, the basic setup is:

You write → GitHub stores it → GitHub Pages publishes it → LinkedIn sends traffic to it.

A simple architecture could be:

LinkedIn Post
     ↓
"Read the full explanation →"
     ↓
Your Blog
     ↓
GitHub Pages
     ↓
Markdown / HTML content
For your use case, I'd keep it simple

You don't need a backend, database, login system, etc.

You could have:

yourusername.github.io
│
├── index.html
├── blogs/
│   ├── cookies-vs-session-storage.html
│   ├── http-vs-https.html
│   └── api-testing-401.html
│
├── css/
│   └── style.css
│
└── assets/
    └── images/